  "summary": "A common resident. Dark brown above, whitish below, with white outer tail feathers and a pale patch on the ear coverts. The yellow shoulder is often vestigial or absent. The male has a pink bill and a dark throat-patch, which may be incomplete. The female has a black bill. The immature has a pink eye-surround and lemon-yellow underparts. The male calls vic-terrr from a regular site in summer, and chatters when guiding to a bees’ nest. The Kemp code RB was left unchanged.",
